  "note": "Annual election of the Aughnacloy Town Commissioners, polled Friday 15 May 1936 (deferred from January 1935). Only five candidates were nominated for nine seats, four Unionists and one Nationalist; they were returned unopposed and four members were to be co-opted (Belfast News-Letter, 30 April 1936, p. 9). Five returned unopposed for nine seats; the remaining four seats were filled by co-option, not by election, so they are not recorded as candidates. Returned unopposed."
